        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you guys say, according to EU GDPR, IPs are private and should be hidden, does it mean that all P2P apps are illegal in EU? :thonking:\n\nIn short, general idea of GDPR, if you somehow know someones IP (or other personal data), and you save and keep it, you should not share it with others. It does not mean that service providers should rebuild ther infrastructure to work somehow w/o using IPs publicly.  It does not mean that service providers should do something to hide your info for you.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
